It's not exactly easy to spot unless you know how the code is
supposed to work.  I had no idea that there was supposed to be
a time delay before getting the "Blecch!  Rotten food!" response,
and I've looked at most of the spoilers and have been in and
out of the Nethack code many times.  I always just figured that
it was intended to be a flat chance -- after all, presumably
the food rations and other food items that you find sitting
around the dungeon have been there for quite a while, so it
isn't unreasonable in most cases to assume that all food items
have a chance of being rotten.  (The horn of plenty case possibly
being an exception).

Probably the most noticable effect is that freshly-killed monster
corpses also have a chance of being rotten, which generally doesn't
make a whole lot of sense.  Since typically if you're going to eat
a monster corpse, you'll eat it immediately after killing it,
I would expect that fixing this would mean many less rotten
food effects from eating corpses.


